<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  updated="Aug 1, 2026"
  description="How conference.contact collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information for site visitors, customers, and directory profiles."
>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Conference.contact operates conference.contact and explains how it
    collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information through its
    Site and Services. This policy applies to site visitors, customers, and
    individuals whose business information is compiled into profiles.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    Conference.contact reserves the right to modify this Privacy Policy at
    any time without prior notice. When material changes are made, we will
    communicate them promptly. Continued use of the Site or Services after
    any update constitutes your acceptance of the revised policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Conference.contact does not knowingly collect personal information from
    individuals under the age of 18, consistent with the eligibility
    requirements in our Terms of Service. We encourage parents and guardians
    to monitor their children's internet usage and to contact us if they
    believe a minor has submitted information through our platform.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>We collect information in the following ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Directly from you — name, email address, company name, phone number,
      and billing address when you register or subscribe.
    </li>
    <li>
      Automatically — through cookies and tracking technologies: device
      information, usage data, and approximate location.
    </li>
    <li>
      From third parties — publicly available sources (event programs,
      speaker rosters, sponsor pages, and similar public materials) used to
      compile business contact profiles in our directory.
    </li>
    <li>
      Payment information — processed entirely through PCI-compliant
      third-party payment processors. We do not store your card details.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <p>We use collected information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide, maintain, and improve our Services</li>
    <li>Create and maintain business contact profiles in our directory</li>
    <li>Process transactions and manage your subscription</li>
    <li>Provide customer support</li>
    <li>Detect and prevent fraud or abuse</li>
    <li>Analyze usage and improve platform performance</li>
    <li>Send service-related and marketing communications</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Disclosure of Information</h2>
  <p>
    We may share your information with service providers who assist in
    operating our platform, with customers who access business profiles in
    our directory, with strategic partners, and as required by law or legal
    process. We do not sell your personal information to unaffiliated third
    parties for their own marketing purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Rights (EEA &amp; UK Users)</h2>
  <p>
    If you are located in the European Economic Area or United Kingdom, you
    have the following rights under GDPR:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access — request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Rectification — ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
    <li>
      Erasure — request deletion of your personal data in certain
      circumstances.
    </li>
    <li>Restriction — ask us to limit how we process your data.</li>
    <li>
      Portability — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable
      format.
    </li>
    <li>Objection — object to processing based on legitimate interests.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, please contact us through our <a
      href="/contact">contact page</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>California Residents (CCPA)</h2>
  <p>
    If you are a California resident, you have additional rights under the
    California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The right to know what categories of personal information we collect,
      the sources, purposes, and third parties we share it with.
    </li>
    <li>
      The right to request deletion of personal information we have
      collected from you.
    </li>
    <li>
      The right to opt out of the sale of your personal information. See our
      <a href="/do-not-sell">Do Not Sell My Info</a> page.
    </li>
    <li>The right not to be discriminated against for exercising your privacy rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>International Data Transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Personal information collected through our Site and Services may be
    stored and processed on servers located in the United States and/or
    Canada. By using our Services, you consent to the transfer, processing,
    and storage of your information outside your country of residence, where
    data protection laws may differ.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    We implement commercially reasonable technical and organizational
    safeguards to protect your personal information against unauthorized
    access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction. However, no method of
    transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, and
    we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use cookies and similar tracking technologies to enhance your
    experience on our Site, analyze usage patterns, and support marketing
    efforts. You may control cookie settings through your browser, though
    disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of our Services.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to exercise your
    data rights, please reach out through our <a href="/contact"
      >contact page</a
    >.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
